└── cooperative async concurrency / monkey-patching backend for Flask-SocketIO
    ├── Candidates : eventlet, gevent
    ├── Used APIs  : monkey_patch
    ├── Pitfalls   : eventlet and gevent use different underlying event loop implementations 
    │   (libev/libuv vs greenlet-based hub) which can cause subtle behavioral differences in 
    │   edge cases; Flask-SocketIO must be configured with the matching async_mode ('eventlet'
    │   vs 'gevent'); Some monkey-patched modules differ slightly between the two libraries 
    │   (e.g., DNS resolution, threading edge cases); eventlet is less actively maintained; 
    │   verify gevent supports all patched modules currently relied upon (e.g., ssl, socket, 
    │   os)
    └── eventlet.monkey_patch() is used to patch stdlib sockets for cooperative concurrency, a
        common backend choice for Flask-SocketIO. gevent provides the same monkey_patch() API 
        and is a well-known drop-in alternative backend supported natively by Flask-SocketIO 
        for the same purpose.

