    ├── Constraints: crypto_required, requires_connector
    └── The file uses Crypto.Cipher.AES to instantiate an AES-CBC cipher object with a key and
        static IV, then calls .encrypt()/.decrypt() on it. Both `cryptography` (via 
        hazmat.primitives.ciphers.Cipher/algorithms.AES/modes.CBC) and `M2Crypto` (via 
        EVP.Cipher with 'aes_128_cbc') expose equivalent low-level AES-CBC primitives that can
        perform the same raw block encryption/decryption, making them functionally viable 
        substitutes for this specific use case. pynacl was considered but rejected since it 
        does not expose raw AES-CBC mode encryption (it is built around XSalsa20-Poly1305 
        secretbox constructions), so it is not a genuine substitute here.

