        (get/set/exists/delete) backed by an embedded on-disk key-value store. plyvel (also a 
        LevelDB binding), rocksdict (RocksDB binding), and lmdb (Lightning Memory-Mapped DB) 
        all provide the same fundamental capability: a persistent, ordered, embedded key-value
        store accessible via simple get/put/delete operations, making them plausible drop-in 
        backends for this abstraction layer.

